  "dimensions": [
    {
      "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#dimension_721651cd",
      "@type": "OverallIntent",
      "instance_name": "overallintent_instance",
      "label": "the overallintent",
      "description": "meme-id: white_people_after_they_put_the_divider_in_between_your_groceries; hasOverallIntent: Hateful; overall-intent-description: The meme uses a photo of Drake, a Black man, in a context that implies he is mocking or expressing satisfaction about a racially charged situation — specifically, the act of 'white people putting a divider between your groceries,' which is a reference to racial segregation in public spaces. The juxtaposition of the image of Drake (a Black celebrity) with the text implies that Black people are being subjected to racial segregation or discrimination in a mundane, everyday setting. This is a hateful meme because it uses a Black person’s image to represent a stereotype or to imply that Black people are being treated as inferior or less than human in a public space. The meme is not merely humorous; it is a form of racial stereotyping and reinforces harmful racial hierarchies by suggesting that Black people are being 'segregated' or 'divided' by white people in a way that is both demeaning and dehumanizing. The meme is also potentially harmful because it normalizes and trivializes racial segregation and discrimination, which can contribute to a culture of racial hostility and misunderstanding. The meme does not contain any direct abusive language or cyberbullying, but it does contain hateful content that targets Black people based on their race.",
      "belongsToAnalysis": {
        "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#analysis_e76e3977"
      },
      "extractionMethod": "llm_extraction_huggingface"
    },
